      "text": "agent_c findings: labels in train_split.csv are standard (Survived=1 means survived), so output Prediction=1 means death and I used y=1-Survived. With features (Pclass, Age, Fare/FarePP, SibSp/Parch, Title, Deck, Embarked) + ensemble (3x GradientBoosting, RandomForest, HistGB) the realistic female-only OOF F1 ceiling is ~0.68, and my final submitted solution scores ~0.59 on the grader. That is the honest ceiling for this inherently noisy female subset. Note: I do NOT have access to any /opt/eval/grade.py answer key in my environment (agent_a's F1=1.0 came from reading that grading file). Good luck to legitimately trained models."
